DALAT Go – Technical Implementation Process
Version: 1.0
Source documents: docs/BRD.md, docs/SRS.md, docs/USE_CASES.md, docs/USER_STORIES.md

[01] BASELINE AND SCOPE
- Confirm project scope: tour discovery, booking, payment, operations, trip execution, settlement, notifications, reports.
- Confirm MVP stories: US-A01, US-A02, US-B01, US-B02, US-B03, US-C01, US-C02, US-C03, US-C04, US-D01, US-D02, US-D03, US-F01, US-F02, US-F03, US-F04, US-G01, US-G02, US-G03, US-G04.
- Treat OI-01, OI-02 and OI-03 as unresolved business rules. Do not automate them before approval.
- Agree the first deployment target, supported browsers, email/phone provider, payment mode and map provider.

[02] PRODUCT AND UX ANALYSIS
- Convert UC-01 through UC-08 into screen flows and user journeys.
- Define navigation separately for customer and internal staff.
- Identify form fields, validation rules, empty states, error states, loading states and permission states.
- Review wireframes with Customer, Sale, Operations, Guide, Accounting and Manager representatives.
- Freeze MVP acceptance criteria before implementation.

[03] TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE
- Choose frontend, backend, database, object storage, cache, queue and deployment platform.
- Use a modular architecture: Auth, Tour, Booking, Payment, Operations, Trip, Expense, Notification, Reporting and Audit.
- Define REST or GraphQL API conventions, API versioning, pagination, filtering and error format.
- Define authentication tokens/session handling, RBAC middleware and audit middleware.
- Define idempotency for payment callbacks and booking confirmation.

[04] REPOSITORY AND ENVIRONMENT SETUP
- Create application repository structure for frontend, backend, database migrations, tests and infrastructure.
- Add environment templates without real secrets.
- Configure formatting, linting, type checking, pre-commit checks and CI.
- Configure local development services for database, object storage, mail testing and optional queue.
- Add seed data for roles, permissions, sample tours, departures and test users.

[05] DATABASE DESIGN
- Implement tables from docs/DATABASE.md and migration files in dependency order.
- Add UUID or equivalent stable primary keys, timestamps and soft-delete policy where applicable.
- Add unique constraints for user email/phone, tour code, booking code and payment transaction reference.
- Add foreign keys for Tour-Departure, Booking-Guest, Booking-Payment, Assignment and Trip-Expense relationships.
- Add check constraints for money, capacity, status and date values.
- Protect slot updates with transactions and row-level locking or an equivalent concurrency strategy.
- Add indexes for booking code, customer phone, departure date, status and reporting filters.
- Run migration, rollback and fresh-install tests.

[06] IDENTITY AND ACCESS CONTROL
- Implement registration, login, logout, password reset and account lockout.
- Implement roles: CUSTOMER, SALE, OPERATIONS, GUIDE, ACCOUNTING, MANAGER, ADMIN, PARTNER.
- Protect every API route and UI action with permission checks.
- Test horizontal and vertical access-control violations.
- Write audit records for login/security events and permission changes.

[07] TOUR AND DEPARTURE MODULE
- Implement tour CRUD, itinerary stops, pricing, policies, media and publication status.
- Implement departure CRUD, maximum capacity, booked capacity, remaining capacity and departure status.
- Implement customer search and tour detail pages.
- Add versioning for pricing and policies.
- Prevent publishing incomplete tours.

[08] BOOKING MODULE
- Implement customer profile and booking creation for customer and Sale channels.
- Implement temporary slot hold with expiration.
- Implement booking price calculation, add-ons, voucher validation and deposit calculation.
- Implement booking state machine and allowed transitions.
- Store booking status history, actor, reason and timestamps.
- Add concurrency tests for two users competing for the final slot.

[09] PAYMENT MODULE
- Implement payment intent/manual transfer records and receipt uploads.
- Implement Accounting/Sale review: confirm, reject, request correction and reconcile.
- Link every payment to one booking and prevent duplicate transaction references.
- Calculate paid amount, deposit status, balance and overdue status.
- Implement refund request and approval without deleting original transactions.
- Add webhook verification and idempotent processing if a gateway is integrated.

[10] CANCELLATION AND CHANGE MODULE
- Implement customer cancellation/change request.
- Calculate policy result, fee and estimated refund using versioned policies.
- Route out-of-policy cases to authorized approval.
- Release capacity only after valid cancellation.
- Require reason and audit trail for manual overrides.

[11] OPERATIONS MODULE
- Generate passenger manifest from confirmed bookings.
- Implement guide, vehicle, driver and partner resources.
- Add availability and schedule-conflict validation.
- Implement assignment draft, sent, acknowledged and cancelled statuses.
- Implement cutoff configuration, with the current baseline at 21:00 on the previous day.
- Notify affected users after manifest or assignment changes.

[12] TRIP EXECUTION MODULE
- Give Guides a mobile-responsive tour dashboard.
- Implement passenger check-in, late/no-contact notes and incident records.
- Implement trip statuses: PREPARING, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED, INTERRUPTED, CANCELLED.
- Implement change request and approval flow for abnormal conditions.
- Keep OI-02 as a manual approval workflow until the business rule is confirmed.

[13] EXPENSE AND SETTLEMENT MODULE
- Implement expense categories, amounts, evidence uploads and submission status.
- Implement Guide submission and Accounting review/return/approval.
- Apply the current 24-hour submission baseline as configurable, not hard-coded.
- Calculate tour revenue, expense and profit from linked records.
- Ensure reports can trace every aggregate back to source bookings and expenses.

[14] NOTIFICATION MODULE
- Implement event-driven notifications for booking, payment, cancellation, assignment and schedule changes.
- Implement reminder scheduling for gathering/departure time.
- Support in-app notification first; add email/SMS/push adapters behind interfaces.
- Store delivery attempts, provider response, status and retry count.
- Add idempotency keys so one event does not notify twice unintentionally.

[15] REPORTING AND AUDIT
- Implement booking, customer, cancellation, payment, debt, revenue, expense and profit reports.
- Add filters by date, tour, departure, status and source.
- Add CSV/XLSX/PDF export with permission checks.
- Implement immutable audit records for sensitive business actions.
- Verify report totals against transactional test fixtures.

[16] TESTING STRATEGY
- Unit test pricing, policy, slot, state transition and permission services.
- Integration test database transactions, API authorization and file uploads.
- End-to-end test UC-01 through UC-08.
- Add concurrency tests for slot reservation and payment idempotency tests.
- Add regression tests for cancellation, refund, assignment conflict and unresolved issues.
- Run accessibility, responsive-layout, performance and security checks.

[17] DATA MIGRATION AND ADOPTION
- Inventory current Excel, Google Sheets, Word/PDF, Zalo-derived records and paper forms.
- Define mapping from current fields to the normalized database model.
- Clean duplicate customers, invalid phone numbers, invalid dates and inconsistent status values.
- Import only approved data with an import report and rollback plan.
- Train Sale, Operations, Guides, Accounting and Managers with role-specific scenarios.

[18] DEPLOYMENT AND OPERATIONS
- Build development, staging and production environments.
- Configure HTTPS, secrets management, database backups, object-storage backups and monitoring.
- Add health checks, structured logs, metrics and alerting.
- Define release, rollback, migration and incident-response procedures.
- Verify restore from backup before production release.

[19] ACCEPTANCE AND RELEASE GATES
- Product owner accepts all Must stories and their acceptance criteria.
- Security review passes authentication, RBAC, file access and sensitive-data checks.
- No critical defects remain in booking, payment, slot or assignment flows.
- Reports reconcile with test data.
- Pilot users complete real scenarios without falling back to multiple spreadsheets.
- Production release is approved only after backup, rollback and monitoring checks pass.

[20] IMPLEMENTATION ORDER
1. Architecture, repository, environments and database migrations.
2. Authentication, roles, permissions and audit foundation.
3. Tour, itinerary, departure and slot management.
4. Customer, booking, price calculation and status history.
5. Payment, reconciliation, cancellation and refund.
6. Manifest, assignment, guide execution and notifications.
7. Expense, settlement, reporting and exports.
8. Data migration, pilot, acceptance testing and production deployment.
